THE PROBLEM (the HUD #2 arm): the 41KB graph-call-manifest catalog is too big to
hold in an agent's head, so even with every tool documented, "which tool answers
this?" is friction the blind-grep reflex skips. comp-which makes the catalog
QUERYABLE: type your actual question, get the canonical comp call -- without
knowing the catalog.

  comp-which "what produces canonical_prices.parquet?"
  comp-which "which lambda serves /api/scoped/advisor-intelligence?"
  comp-which "what breaks if I change build_dashboard?"

Two layers:
 1. CURATED high-confidence rules = CVO #3 baseline's ranked question->tool map
    (bdf7a0a9a) -- the high-traffic question classes get the exact, vetted call.
 2. MANIFEST-FUZZY backstop = keyword-overlap score over graph-call-manifest.yaml's
    use_case entries -> comprehensive + auto-updates as tools are added.

Read-only, deterministic, ASCII-only. Tune the curated rules to CVO's post-hook
re-measure (which redirects agents accept vs ignore).
"""
